; Integer functions given a single float, a rational, a character or a symbol in each
; integer position, interpreted and compiled (microcode 2001).  A single float is an
; immediate whose pointer field holds its bits, past the 28-bit address space; GET-ANY-BIG
; and GET-BIG-FIX (sys/ucadr/uc-arith.lisp) started a read at it before ASSURE-BIGNUM tested
; its type, so GCD, \\, LCM, \, REMAINDER and CLI:REM with a float halted the machine at
; PGF-MAP-MISS; they signal the wrong-type error now, as for a symbol or a rational.  A
; character counts as its code, as everywhere in this system's integer functions; MOD and
; %DIV take floats and rationals; the logical functions, ASH and LDB never reached that code
; and are here as they answer.  Microcode that halts answers none after it.
(gcd 12 18) => 6
